//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- controls: the confidence axis
//
// These are not recall queries and are deliberately excluded from recall@1 and
// recall@k — they carry no `expected_session_prefix` because five of the six
// are asserting that the right answer is **nothing**. They are judged on their
// own by `--controls`, and a failure there fails the run.
//
// Why they exist. The agent audit of 23 aug 2026 found that `find` could not
// tell a topic the archive answers from one it has never heard of: 0.01836
// against 0.01639 on the reference archive, 1.12x apart, because reciprocal
// rank fusion is a function of rank alone. T10.1 added a second axis and a
// floor. These are what stop it rotting: one query the archive answers, which
// must come back `strong`; four topics that are definitively absent while every
// content word of each (or, for `limiting`, its stem) is present in the corpus
// somewhere else, which must come back with zero rows; and one string of
// invented words, which must come back with
// zero rows for the simpler reason that fts5 finds no term at all.
//
// The audit's own controls could not be reused. Its nonsense string had been
// written down in a document that was then indexed, so by the time anyone
// re-ran it the archive contained the session that typed it and the control
// matched itself. That is the failure mode a control has: publication. These
// are safe against it in the only way that lasts — they are scored against
// `evals/fixture/`, a corpus generated by `scripts/make-eval-corpus.mjs` from
// a template grid, which nothing anybody types can ever get into.
//
// T10.10 added the last three. `plans/06` asks the set to cover the case where
// the honest answer is that the corpus does not contain it, and `control:
// "no-match"` is the format's existing way of writing that gold down — a
// no-answer query needs no `expected_session_prefix` because there is no
// session to name. Each of the three is a conjunction of two topics the corpus
// really has, describing a session it really does not: the words are all
// present and the thing is absent, which is the only kind of absence that is
// hard.
{"query": "pgbouncer transaction pooling", "control": "strong", "class": "control", "note": "[keyword] TRUE TOPIC, short and distinctive — the corpus has a session about exactly this. Must return at least one row at `strong`. This is the control that fails if the floor is ever raised until nothing survives it: an honest empty is only worth having if the tool can still say yes."}
{"query": "kubernetes ingress payment service", "control": "no-match", "class": "control", "note": "[keyword] ABSENT TOPIC, and the point is that its words are not absent — the corpus has sessions about payments and about services, so bm25 returns rows and ranks them, and before T10.1 the top one scored inside 12% of a true phrase hit. Must return ZERO rows. If this ever returns anything, the cliff has become a ranking again."}
{"query": "vondrelic pashtomeer", "control": "no-match", "class": "control", "note": "[keyword] INVENTED WORDS, generated for this file and used nowhere else. Must return ZERO rows, and it already did before T10.1 — fts5 finds no term, so there is nothing to rank. It is here as a regression control rather than as a fix: the audit reported that gibberish returned ten confident rows, that claim did not reproduce on uncontaminated tokens, and this is what keeps it from becoming true later."}
{"query": "dark mode for the invoice pdf", "control": "no-match", "class": "control", "note": "[sentence] ABSENT TOPIC, added by T10.10. Dark and mode are in the design-tokens session; invoice and pdf are in a deleted api thread about a pdf job running out of heap. No session in the corpus is about theming an invoice, and no single session holds more than half the query. Must return ZERO rows."}
{"query": "rate limiting the sitemap generator", "control": "no-match", "class": "control", "note": "[sentence] ABSENT TOPIC, added by T10.10. Rate and limited are in the outbound webhook session (limiting itself appears nowhere, which is the one place this control leans on a stem rather than a word); sitemap and generator are in a deleted seo thread. Nothing rate limits a sitemap anywhere in the corpus. Must return ZERO rows."}
{"query": "bluetooth on the checkout page", "control": "no-match", "class": "control", "note": "[sentence] ABSENT TOPIC, added by T10.10. Bluetooth belongs to a devices ghost and checkout to four separate web and api sessions, which makes this the hardest of the three: the second half of the query has a large, genuinely relevant-looking neighbourhood and the first half has none. Must return ZERO rows."}
